# TradingView Strategy 461 TS M15 Sweep

## Source
- Source: [[sources/tradingview-mechanical-strategy-scripts]]
- Page / Timestamp: TradingView script `Strategy 461 - TS M15`, author handle `Fran_Pineda`, open-source strategy, accessed 2026-05-22, page shows May 7, https://www.tradingview.com/script/8Evzyktw/

## Mechanics

### Entry
Use M15 baseline, source market XAUUSD.

- Long setup:
  - Previous candle is bearish.
  - Current candle trades below the previous candle low.
  - Current candle does not trade above the previous candle high.
  - Current candle closes bullish.
  - Current close is back above the previous candle low.
  - Optional EMA(200) filter enabled: close is above EMA(200).
- Short setup:
  - Previous candle is bullish.
  - Current candle trades above the previous candle high.
  - Current candle does not trade below the previous candle low.
  - Current candle closes bearish.
  - Current close is back below the previous candle high.
  - Optional EMA(200) filter enabled: close is below EMA(200).

### Exit
- Take profit: selected RR multiple of stop distance.
- Baseline RR: 1.5R.
- Exit only by stop or take profit.

### Stop Loss
- Long stop: below the sweep candle low plus configurable tick buffer.
- Short stop: above the sweep candle high plus configurable tick buffer.

### Position Sizing
V5 default: fixed-risk $1,000 for P2 baseline, one position per symbol/magic.

### Zusatzliche Filter
- Session filter optional; baseline tests London+NY active windows on XAUUSD and major indices.
- Skip signals where sweep candle range is less than 0.25 * ATR(14) or greater than 2.5 * ATR(14).

## Concepts (what kind of strategy is this)
- [[concepts/liquidity-sweep]] - entry requires a one-candle stop-run through the prior candle extreme.
- [[concepts/reversal]] - candle must close back with opposite directional strength.
- [[concepts/trend-filter]] - optional EMA(200) prevents counter-trend entries.

